[CRITICAL] SCAN-001 Package file could not be analyzed: demo
    'tests/fixtures/malicious/install-plus-eq/demo' is declared by install= but does not exist; makepkg would refuse it, and the declared scriptlet could not be reviewed. Content that was not analyzed cannot be reported clean; a payload can hide behind exactly this.
    Recommendation: Do not install. Inspect the file by hand; a legitimate package has no reason to ship an oversized, unreadable, or symlinked script.
    Reference: CWE-693

[CRITICAL] ATOMIC-002 Node/Bun package manager in install hook (install script)
    Invokes npm/pnpm/yarn/bun (or the npx/bunx runners) to install or run packages from an install hook. The June 2026 'Atomic Arch' campaign added post-install hooks running `npm install atomic-lockfile` / `bun install js-digest`. Legitimate packages never fetch or execute npm/bun packages during the install phase. `npm ci`, `npm rebuild`, `npm exec`, `pnpm dlx`, `yarn dlx`, and the bare `npx <pkg>` / `bunx <pkg>` runners all fetch-and-run lifecycle/remote code just like `install`.
    Location: tests/fixtures/malicious/install-plus-eq/demo.scr:2
    Code:   npm install -g evilpkg
    Recommendation: Install scripts must never fetch or install npm/bun packages. Inspect the PKGBUILD diff and report the package to the AUR maintainers.
    Reference: CWE-494

[HIGH] META-007 install= cannot be statically resolved
    The install scriptlet name is not a plain value the scanner can resolve (install modified by += / [i]= / read / printf -v). makepkg runs whichever file it names as the package's install scriptlet, so every file beside the PKGBUILD was scanned as a possible scriptlet.
    Code: install=install modified by += / [i]= / read / printf -v
    Recommendation: Do not install. Use a literal `install=<pkgname>.install` and review the file it names.
    Reference: CWE-426

[MEDIUM] META-005 install= points outside the package
    install=demo is not a plain `<name>.install` file in the package directory (it contains a path, `..`, or a non-.install name). makepkg runs this scriptlet as part of the package; an out-of-tree path is a way to run an unexpected file.
    Code: install=demo
    Recommendation: Use a plain `<pkgname>.install` file shipped alongside the PKGBUILD.
    Reference: CWE-426



